  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Step 1 parts kept unchanged: 3 FSRs (the circuit image uses FSRs), 3 x 10k resistors, 7 jumper wires, Uno, breadboard.",
   "The image shows the breadboard with rows a-e in its lower half; these are bank 't' in the catalogue naming. Top rails: tp = + (red line), tn = - (black line); bottom rails: bp = + (red line), bn = - (black line).",
   "Rail hole numbers (tp.1, tn.2, bp.4/12/21, bn.6/16/24, etc.) are approximated from the image; any hole on the same rail is electrically equivalent.",
   "Each channel is a voltage divider: FSR from 5V (bottom + rail) to a column, 10k resistor from that column to GND (bottom - rail), and a yellow wire from that column to the analog input. A0 goes to column 24, A1 to column 16 and A2 to column 6, as traced in the image.",
   "Power: Uno 5V to the top + rail, Uno GND to the top - rail, and two short jumpers carry both rails to the bottom rails.",
   "FSR pin 1 is the lead going to the + rail and pin 2 the lead going to the column; the FSR is symmetric so the choice is arbitrary."
  ]
 },
